# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ground rule 1 of REVERSING.md: no proprietary bytes in git.
#
# The SoftVoice DLLs belong to SoftVoice, Inc. The rule tables and coefficient
# data inside them are extracted at BUILD time, by tools/extract_*.py, from a
# copy the user already owns, into the CMake build tree. Neither the DLLs nor
# anything generated from them may ever be committed. These patterns are a
# backstop, not permission to put such a file in the source tree.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.DLL
*.dll
build/
build-*/
build_*/
cmake-build-*/

# Output of the build-time table extractors, wherever it lands. Unanchored on
# the left: CMake writes plain base_data.c into the build tree, which a
# *_base_data.c pattern would miss.
*lang_data.c
*base_data.c

# Compiled artifacts carry the extracted tables inside them just as plainly as
# the generated .c does.
*.a
*.so
*.dylib
*.o
*.obj

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
